{"kind":"report","text":"Approved — DESIGN ONLY, Jam revision 8 at 0861580ea3b3d3c50a3f9a055d5614daf1cbfa17, tree 36d862344b4ae1361ee26abea3e811d5b01593d5. Evidence for request 9ce8533f0fe1d8eefa0e7e864dc860f3b3969c35; no implementation closure or adoption.\n\nThe R7 timing P2 is repaired. A lookahead value is recorded at its entry and becomes active at its own derived effect bar. Scheduling reads the value active at the entry's time, rather than the latest recorded slot or a pending value. Lower-sequence pending tempo segments remain on the boundary schedule; increasing/decreasing lookahead, multiple pending changes, same-bar sequence ties and already assigned bars have one stated treatment. A pattern naming a pending interpretation cannot start before that interpretation.\n\nPlanner assertion 7fbe7c43, personally FULL inspected, explicitly accepts the room-wide nondecreasing effect-bar floor and its possible delay to an unrelated instrument after a decrease. This resolves the independent report's earlier pending-owner-disposition qualification; it does not constitute whole-note adoption. Same-bar bunching, cross-part delay and mixed tempo/lookahead cases belong in the owed musical fixture. No distinct start bar for every entry or measured latency is claimed. First-origin/count-in bootstrap and solo recording remain explicit open design questions.\n\nArchitecture: signed room history provides the replay inputs; musical scheduling is application code, separate from Artroom's judgment replay and the nonauthoritative live layer. P9 now correctly separates a mutable Jam application rules item from repository platform:rules. The actual definition, founding item, grant/guard wiring and hosted room remain unbuilt; general value-form support is conditional, not a hosted demonstration.\n\nSecurity: the stage authors nobody's authoritative acts; the person and each agent sign their own. Live cues/audio carry no platform authority. Audio location, hosted-model use, membership permissions and read-session renewal retain their stated owner duties; no private audio or provider was inspected.\n\nSimplification: one active-lookahead meaning and one owner-accepted ordering rule replace the conflicting pending-value rule. Historical configurations and bars remain derived from recorded entries, with no mutable active flag. The 2–4 second wait is properly qualified by active lookahead and absence of an earlier hold; the eight-second response target and human judgment remain separate acceptance tests.\n\nChecker and an independent reader each freshly personally FULL read the complete current note (79843 bytes), complete R7-to-R8 native U3 (48476 bytes) and same-head plan 021 (8008 bytes): 136327 bytes, 2183 LF, 16 gap-free bounded displays each. Checker also FULL read the report and ledger; all native identities/hashes/coverage verified. Native diff changes only the note; both package trees are 166c2676af34078b14c654151c36fd6c0cc9bd63. Seal /tmp/artroom-checker-jam-r8-0861-ordinary-root-binding.json, 7209 bytes, SHA256 e4930afca8f1ca24a11b37148ea6ce6e7083467376312d821bfbc7b489fa19b1.\n\nNo tests/gates/project execution/simulations/generated histories/audio/provider probes/source changes. The five real phrases by two people, human recognition/musical judgment, browser and deployed timing, model/license/cost decision, all nine platform gaps, full definition/application/IA/I3/runtime/custody, indefinite-session behavior and all five capacity dimensions remain owed. Approval of this design text closes none of those implementation or acceptance duties.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f469c2ce00d1464bf2d54c2b72814f619b0fcc09","binding":"evidence-only","head":"0861580ea3b3d3c50a3f9a055d5614daf1cbfa17","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:87ebe00a58347abcebcfbe5b9c390a4c831f3600\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sh